# A3 Synexia mastery custody

## Invariant

Reusable Atomize/Patternize/Document/Convergence recipes are mastered in
`hsoliwal/com.synexia`.

M3JDK21 is a target consumer. It may retain compatibility mirrors, frozen proof fixtures and
JDK-specific adapters, but its mastery laboratory and recipe catalogue must resolve reusable
FILE-local convergence recipes through the Synexia-owned package.

## A3 mastery consumer

The compiler-driven A3 laboratory executes:

- `com.synexia.rewrite.atom.M3AtomizePureIntReturnRecipe`
- `com.synexia.rewrite.atom.M3PatternizePureIntAtomRecipe`

The laboratory still owns only JDK-side proof:

- hostile Java fixture generation;
- permutations and multi-pass schedules;
- in-memory javac after each application;
- public/protected contract comparison;
- behavior comparison;
- code-looking string/comment/text-block preservation;
- regex x string matrix evidence;
- equal-subset convergence;
- second-pass fixed point.

Portable recipe semantics remain Synexia-owned.

## Catalogue

The five reusable pure-int recipe rows in `m3/tooling/recipe-catalogue.tsv` resolve to the
`com.synexia.rewrite.atom` package:

1. inventory;
2. atomize;
3. patternize;
4. document;
5. convergence.

The legacy `com.m3.rewrite.atom` compatibility mirrors are not deleted by this packet. Removing
them requires separate consumer proof and canonical readback.

## Recipe-first delivery

This custody change is delivered as two exact FILE atoms:

- Java: `M3HashPinnedJavaSnapshotRecipe(a3-synexia-mastery-custody)`;
- text: `M3Jdk21HashPinnedTextSnapshotRecipe(a3-synexia-mastery-custody-text)`.

The composition is `com.m3.a3.SynexiaMasteryCustodyDelivery`.

Both exact preimages are hash-pinned. Replay on the postimages is a no-op.

## Product boundary

No OpenJDK `src/` or `test/` product file changes.

No JDK public API, HotSpot ABI, JNI ABI, class-file format, JEP disposition or backport packet changes.

OpenJDK `configure -> make -> jtreg -> runtime` remains the product oracle.
